      "evidence_sha256": "2e3fd5e125a8c8775add29edafadb991ed8698504520ac42a659bd47314f9c04",
      "assessment": "R4 G1 used only automatic history and paired evidence. It correctly recognizes latest Mean 4.190014 and incumbent 4.214778, but mixes the positive own-lineage change of 0.027844 with the incumbent advantage of 0.024764. H1 [7,5,5,5] is a reversion; H2 [7,6,6,5] is called an untested combination although it can only know its private lineage and previous public reflection. Neither proposal is selected for R5.",
      "decision_update": "Label every comparator and the visibility scope of an untested claim. Reuse prior mechanics as hypotheses, not current measurements. Keep Mean as the objective and concentration as a sensitivity diagnostic; do not introduce a compulsory median improvement or call the current Top10 an established ceiling.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The private agent cannot see that a sibling evaluated H2 in the same wave, so absence from its own lineage is not an error; a global untested claim is unsupported. Unselected proposals have no R5 outcome and cannot be credited with a sampled result.",
