    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r04/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "bf40e571d4285f3dbe1fea26fd58125395845f0cf1221af0dd4377640dcca715",
      "assessment": "R4 G2 obtains a direct own-lineage R3-to-R4 mean change of only +0.00002648. Its auto latest-to-incumbent +0.025850 and all-positive quartiles mean incumbent superiority, but it calls these a treatment gain. The requested subgroups are stratified by latest, not preintervention as claimed. It also calls the final interval most opposing when the third interval has the more negative measured cosine. H1 [8,6,6,5] and H2 [7,6,6,4] are selected.",
      "decision_update": "Derive subgroup reference population and direction from actual tool arguments. Distinguish a descriptive treatment-defined stratum from a preintervention stratum. Use exact interval metrics, and replace unsupported 0.03 noise bands with observed response and uncertainty limitations. Preserve the direct lineage query as a useful check.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "R5 H1 Mean 4.151162 falls about 0.037766 below its source group, while H2 gives 4.188957, about +0.000029. These outcomes do not support the early-escalation forecast, but changing selected restart parents limits cross-round causal attribution.",
