      "assessment": "R4 G3 correctly identifies the 0.024801 incumbent advantage over latest [7,5,5,5], but treats failure to beat a per-chain selected incumbent as evidence that the early dose is not positive. Its H1 [6,5,5,5] is selected for R5 and produces Mean 4.162146, about 0.027831 below its source result; H2 [7,5,6,5] is not selected. No new tools beyond automatic history and paired evidence were requested.",
      "decision_update": "Separate the system-retention comparator from a schedule-effect comparator. Keep the decrement as a local test, while evaluating its actual source contrast and changed parents. Replace invented 0.03/0.2 cutoffs and a mandatory median gain with full Mean plus influence and quality diagnostics.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The selected incumbent can exceed every fixed schedule by construction, so a deficit to it cannot alone refute a useful schedule. The R5 decrement loses Mean relative to the source but is not a same-wave causal comparison; H2 has no new R5 result.",
