    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r04/G4",
      "evidence_sha256": "0f53d6fd435d4109227a64c1419388738e8b586d11312a5c3c1069fd80ca7536",
      "assessment": "R4 G4 explicitly reconciles opposite tool directions correctly, a useful improvement over earlier rounds. Nevertheless it quotes the fixed Mean as 4.173 rather than 4.164944, concludes one-core geometry must be too coarse without testing that mechanism, and says it will stop interpreting pooled Means. H1 [6,5,6,5] is selected for R5 and gives 4.162170; H2 [5,6,6,5] is not selected. Its equal-tick window contrast is sensible but not both arms executed.",
      "decision_update": "Preserve explicit sign reconciliation while retaining the requested Mean objective. Acknowledge that small physical displacement can coexist with large discrete score changes. Treat core-coverage sufficiency and proxy mismatch as unresolved alternatives, not a reason to declare an entire permitted control range inert.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The selected H1 is lower than its source by about 0.002774 and shows almost the same R5 Mean as [6,5,5,5]. This supports a small local third-window response in that context, not a universal conclusion that window location cannot matter.",
